  "title": "Perfekt — Talking About the Past",
  "explanation": "The **Perfekt** tense is the most common way to talk about the past in spoken German. It's formed with a conjugated *haben* or *sein* plus a past participle (usually *ge-...-t* or *ge-...-en*) pushed to the end of the sentence.",
  "examples": [
    { "de": "Ich habe Deutsch gelernt.", "en": "I learned German." },
    { "de": "Wir sind nach Berlin gefahren.", "en": "We traveled to Berlin." },
    { "de": "Er hat das Buch gelesen.", "en": "He read the book." }
  ],
